    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42572" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sāpis</span></b> , is, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in
				Cisalpine Gaul and Umbria</i>, <i>between Ravenna
				and Ariminum</i>, now <i>the Savio</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 15,
				20, § 115</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			450</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 2, 406</span></i> (al.
			Isapis).—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sāpĭnĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of the Sapis</i>, <i>Sapinian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					31, 2, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">33, 37,
		1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
